From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] quartz: implement the VMR7/VMR9 configuration, mixer and pin interfaces

The VMR filters have no real D3D/DirectDraw engine to drive until a pin is
connected, so each stubbed interface now keeps the documented state with the
documented defaults, ranges and HRESULTs.

VMR9: IVMRFilterConfig9 (rendering prefs masked by RenderPrefs9_Mask, 1..16
streams, image compositor kept and released with the filter), IVMRMixerControl9
(per-stream alpha 0..1 default 1, z-order default = stream index, normalized
output rect default 0,0,1,1, background color, E_INVALIDARG for a stream that
does not exist; ProcAmp calls report VFW_E_VMR_NO_PROCAMP_HW after validating
size, flags and stream), IVMRMixerBitmap9 (alpha bitmap validated, stored,
partially updated, VFW_E_WRONG_STATE before one is set), IVMRWindowlessControl9
(ideal sizes, border color, DisplayModeChanged, GetCurrentImage, aspect mode
validated), IVMRMonitorConfig9 (monitor index checked against the monitor count,
uDevID reported), the COPP calls keep returning VFW_E_NO_COPP_HW without a FIXME.

VMR7: the same for IVMRFilterConfig, IVMRMonitorConfig (monitor GUIDs),
IVMRWindowlessControl (aspect mode, border color, color key, repaint, display
mode change, GetCurrentImage which converts the last frame to a 32-bit bitmap
for RGB and the packed and planar YUV formats), IVMRSurfaceAllocatorNotify
(SetDDrawDevice/ChangeDDrawDevice hold the device, RestoreDDrawSurfaces,
NotifyEvent, SetBorderColor), and the default allocator-presenter (start/stop
presenting, AdviseNotify, the windowless control state, 24-bit surfaces).

Both pins: IAMVideoAccelerator reports no accelerator and no frame session
(VFW_E_WRONG_STATE), IOverlay stores palette, color key and the advise sink and
reports the window rectangles, VFW_E_WRONG_STATE without a window. todo_wine
marks that started passing are removed from tests/vmr7.c.
